"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[97609],{97609:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n\\n<center>\\n<TvCard\\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/screen/game-of-blood-x.jpg\\"\\n          title=\\"Game of Blood X (2026)\\"\\n          release_date=\\"2026-07-03\\"\\n          episode_count=10\\n          genres=[\\"Reality\\"]\\n          rating=4.0\\n          tags=\\"tv\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nUnlike previous seasons, this season was <mark>explicitly designed as a team competition</mark>.  \\nBringing together familiar faces from past seasons, alumni from other survival shows, and newcomers stepping into this kind of brain survival show for the first time into five competing teams felt quite refreshing.  \\n\\nWith multiple teams going head-to-head, forming alliances between teams might seem easy at first glance, but in reality, it felt far trickier.  \\nEven if teams form a tight alliance, just one member betraying the pact or harboring different motives can shatter the entire alliance in an instant.  \\n\\nMoreover, dividing roles and aligning strategies within a team framework made the <mark>gameplay elements relying on intellect</mark> feel much deeper than in individual competitions.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nHowever, as the show progressed toward the later stages, certain individuals\' aggressive behavior and excessive over-immersion made viewing quite uncomfortable and caused much frowning throughout.  \\nOf course, given the nature of an extreme survival show where winning and losing are at stake, unreasonable demands and shameless attitudes might be an inevitable byproduct.  \\nUltimately, the fatigue and discomfort stirred by a few participants felt like a double-edged sword that this genre must inevitably bear.  \\n\\nWhile everyone praised the elaborate team play and suspenseful battles of wits up through the early-to-mid stages, it was impossible not to feel drained as it devolved into emotional clashes in the latter half.  \\nIn particular, the attitudes that went beyond strategic villainy crossed the line too far to simply defend as the \\"charm of survival shows.\\"  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nI felt that the production team\'s intervention or rule adjustments should have been more nuanced, and perhaps it would have felt less frustrating had it been an individual match.  \\nIn the end, compared to the great, novel setup of a five-team showdown, the emotional exhaustion among the players seemed to undermine the game\'s overall quality.  \\n\\nWhile it definitely delivered entertainment and immersive suspense, the lingering aftertaste left something to be desired.  \\nEven if it captured buzz and attention, it will likely be remembered as a bittersweet season that leaves behind quite a bitter emotional residue."}')}}]);